Subject: Fix: redraw resting goal nets (issue #19)
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509

A fix of the original game, always on and without a switch (owner decision,
2026-10-12). It lives in the tweak series so the faithful series stays retail.

DrawableNetMesh::Render rebuilds a goal net's mesh only while the net
simulation is active (a ball in the net) or after a replay frame changed the
net's recorded visibility; a resting net keeps drawing the mesh it built last.
Every goal resets both nets (NetMesh::Reset) when its replay starts
(StartAutoReplay) and when it ends (ReplayChoreo::Finish). The simulated net
returns to its rest shape and turns inactive, but the drawn mesh is not
invalidated, so the shape last drawn in the replay stayed on screen until the
ball next entered that net and it was redrawn at once (issue #19: a net left
bulged outward after a goal). The original code does the same.

The net is now rebuilt every frame, as the original already does while a ball
is in it. Only the drawing changes; the net simulation, replays and sync logs
are unchanged. A resting net now also follows the world darkening, which the
original applied only when it rebuilt the mesh.

